                  "formattedValue": "16 November 2026 update: Page published and live-verified with the complete original abstract, unchanged native files and BibTeX, scholarly metadata, and working desktop/fresh-mobile PDF readers. Native v1.0.0, declared 12 October and created 13 October UTC remain distinct. No corresponding article was identified in 47 authenticated current GitHub Pages HTML bodies; no unrelated route or asset was redirected. This bounded lookup is not a history-wide absence claim. Direct live file bytes match the originals; no successful native download-dialog check is claimed. Publication evidence: https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/blob/4437b1f3b853983daf0616bfb1e8af23b542c647/research_website_catalogue_20261024/verification/root-knudson-annular-publication-20261116.json . Bounded legacy evidence: https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/blob/4437b1f3b853983daf0616bfb1e8af23b542c647/research_website_catalogue_20261024/verification/root-annular-martin-legacy-adoption-20261116.json\n\nEarlier inventory note:\nFull original smooth-annulus counterexample passed substantive source-first, independent and adversarial review. The normalized minimal Martin kernel at -1 in 1<|z|<e is strictly below the positive-harmonic envelope throughout a punctured neighborhood of exp(1/2). Exact Green limit/minimality and four-competitor all-direction gap prove local isolation, without numeric sampling. Original Problem 7.42 and classical punctured-disc qualification checked; no claim about farther contact, historical firstness or current worldwide openness. No repair, narrowing or qualifying follow-up. Page preparing; canonical blank until live verification. Evidence: https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/blob/cac0684d32627df799054cc2fe24180618597cb4/research_website_catalogue_20261024/verification/root-clearance-23332261-20261116.json",
                  "userEnteredValue": {
                    "stringValue": "16 November 2026 update: Page published and live-verified with the complete original abstract, unchanged native files and BibTeX, scholarly metadata, and working desktop/fresh-mobile PDF readers. Native v1.0.0, declared 12 October and created 13 October UTC remain distinct. No corresponding article was identified in 47 authenticated current GitHub Pages HTML bodies; no unrelated route or asset was redirected. This bounded lookup is not a history-wide absence claim. Direct live file bytes match the originals; no successful native download-dialog check is claimed. Publication evidence: https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/blob/4437b1f3b853983daf0616bfb1e8af23b542c647/research_website_catalogue_20261024/verification/root-knudson-annular-publication-20261116.json . Bounded legacy evidence: https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/blob/4437b1f3b853983daf0616bfb1e8af23b542c647/research_website_catalogue_20261024/verification/root-annular-martin-legacy-adoption-20261116.json\n\nEarlier inventory note:\nFull original smooth-annulus counterexample passed substantive source-first, independent and adversarial review. The normalized minimal Martin kernel at -1 in 1<|z|<e is strictly below the positive-harmonic envelope throughout a punctured neighborhood of exp(1/2). Exact Green limit/minimality and four-competitor all-direction gap prove local isolation, without numeric sampling. Original Problem 7.42 and classical punctured-disc qualification checked; no claim about farther contact, historical firstness or current worldwide openness. No repair, narrowing or qualifying follow-up. Page preparing; canonical blank until live verification. Evidence: https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/blob/cac0684d32627df799054cc2fe24180618597cb4/research_website_catalogue_20261024/verification/root-clearance-23332261-20261116.json"
                  },
                  "effectiveValue": {
                    "stringValue": "16 November 2026 update: Page published and live-verified with the complete original abstract, unchanged native files and BibTeX, scholarly metadata, and working desktop/fresh-mobile PDF readers. Native v1.0.0, declared 12 October and created 13 October UTC remain distinct. No corresponding article was identified in 47 authenticated current GitHub Pages HTML bodies; no unrelated route or asset was redirected. This bounded lookup is not a history-wide absence claim. Direct live file bytes match the originals; no successful native download-dialog check is claimed. Publication evidence: https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/blob/4437b1f3b853983daf0616bfb1e8af23b542c647/research_website_catalogue_20261024/verification/root-knudson-annular-publication-20261116.json . Bounded legacy evidence: https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/blob/4437b1f3b853983daf0616bfb1e8af23b542c647/research_website_catalogue_20261024/verification/root-annular-martin-legacy-adoption-20261116.json\n\nEarlier inventory note:\nFull original smooth-annulus counterexample passed substantive source-first, independent and adversarial review. The normalized minimal Martin kernel at -1 in 1<|z|<e is strictly below the positive-harmonic envelope throughout a punctured neighborhood of exp(1/2). Exact Green limit/minimality and four-competitor all-direction gap prove local isolation, without numeric sampling. Original Problem 7.42 and classical punctured-disc qualification checked; no claim about farther contact, historical firstness or current worldwide openness. No repair, narrowing or qualifying follow-up. Page preparing; canonical blank until live verification. Evidence: https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/blob/cac0684d32627df799054cc2fe24180618597cb4/research_website_catalogue_20261024/verification/root-clearance-23332261-20261116.json"
