                {
                  "formattedValue": "Full original max-degree-four graph and probability theorem passed source-first, independent and adversarial review: rough isometry C=100, p_c<=9/10, and at p=19/20 probability of at least two infinite clusters exceeds 2200741829/6461571200>1/3. Exact quadrant dual parity, all-start/all-length weak paths and independent infinite-event families prove the result; the finite native checker passed once as supplementary evidence. Problem 9.6 omits its p quantifier: the paper refutes its declared all-supercritical interpretation, without uniquely attributing author intent or refuting near-one uniqueness. No repair, narrowing or qualifying follow-up. Page preparing; canonical blank until live verification. Evidence: https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/blob/7492e3db011862a0c1500abe9dcca5023bfb43fb/research_website_catalogue_20261024/verification/root-clearance-23573603-20261116.json",
